ting; formal register.\" Count: Polite1 thanks2 for3 waiting;4 formal5 register. 5 words.\n\n13. \"Discussing pet policies; “depende” signals a condition.\" Count: Discussing1 pet2 policies;3 “depende”4 signals5 a6 condition. 6 words.\n\n14. \"Reassuring about pets; informal but polite statement.\" Count: Reassuring1 about2 pets;3 informal4 but5 polite6 statement. 6 words.\n\n15. \"Polite pause before deciding; “déjeme” is a formal request.\" Count: Polite1 pause2 before3 deciding;4 “déjeme”5 is6 a7 formal8 request. 8 words.\n\n16. \"Formal service greeting; useful in shops or hotels.\" Count: Formal1 service2 greeting;3 useful4 in5 shops6 or7 hotels. 7 words.\n\n17. \"Asking for feedback after a viewing; neutral tone.\" Count: Asking1 for2 feedback3 after4 a5 viewing;6 neutral7 tone. 7 words.\n\n18. \"Commenting on food; “muy buena” shows strong positive opinion.\" Count: Commenting1 on2 food;3 “muy4 buena”5 shows6 strong7 positive8 opinion. 8 words.\n\n19. \"Ordering non‑carbonated water; useful restaurant phrase.\" Count: Ordering1 non‑carbonated2 water;3 useful4 restaurant5 phrase. 5 words.\n\n20. \"Checking weather; “por cierto” introduces side question.\" Count: Checking1 weather;2 “por3 cierto”4 introduces5 side6 question. 6 words.\n\nAll within limit.\n\nNow the sheet content.\n\nFormat.\n\nNow we need to embed the sheet in a delegate command.\n\nWill produce via assistant.\n\nNow we must send the first delegate command to save the sheet file, and after receipt we will handle tag question.\n\nSo we need to send a delegate command to knowledge-agent with the full sheet text.\n\nTo construct, we must be careful about quoting and typographic apostrophe. Also no straight apostrophes.\n\nPotential issue: In phrase #4 translation includes \"I’m\". That's using typographic ’. That's fine.\n\nAlso phrase #5 translation includes \"So‑so\" which contains hyphen (en dash). Acceptable.\n\nNow produce instruction string.\n\nWill include the sheet text verbatim, with mark